Configuration parameters such as hot_standby_feedback, delay settings, and memory allocations pull against one another. If you enable hot_standby_feedback to prevent analytical queries from being canceled by vacuum operations on the primary, you risk table bloat on the write leader. If you disable it, long-running batch queries fail when underlying rows are cleaned up.

